fact WorkItem(id: "WI-294", description: some(value: "Scala loader/typer: port operation-body loading + type-hint consumption (WI-288 follow-up). Builds the Scala-side operation loading that WI-288's parser hints feed into; gated behind the scaland Term->Value resolver migration (mirror of rustland WI-246: occurrence-native SLD, Value::Node, Rc<NodeOccurrence>) so it lands on the right substrate. Currently in scaland: convertExprTerm + its load* helpers (loadLetExpr, loadApplyOrConstructor, etc.) are DEAD CODE — no caller; operations are only defined as symbols in scan pass 1 (Loader.scala:125-134), never loaded into the KB as OperationInfo facts; and there is NO native-Scala typer (the 'dual typer' = Rust typer + the self-hosted typer in stdlib/anthill/reflect/typing.anthill run via SLD). Scope: (1) Phase-2 operation handler in Loader.loadItems that builds anthill.reflect.OperationInfo facts (name/params/return_type/effects/requires/ensures/body/type_params), mirroring rustland kb/load.rs:5569-5708; (2) wire convertExprTerm as the operation-body converter; (3) item 1 of WI-288 — loadLetExpr: thread the 'type_name' named-arg into Expr.let_expr.type_name (Some/None); (4) item 2 of WI-288 — loadApplyOrConstructor: strip the 'type_args' named-arg and route as Expr.apply/ho_apply.type_args (cons-list of reflect type_arg(name,value)); constructor has no type_args (drop); (5) item 4 of WI-288 — register operation type-params as scoped Sort symbols in an operation scope (kb.symbols.define + addTypeParam), mirror rustland load.rs:357-362, and allocate per-param Vars published in OperationInfo.type_params; (6) typer-side seeding of call-site type_args onto op type-param Vars (rustland typing.rs reseed_type_params_from_call_args) — only meaningful once the typing.anthill rules run over loaded OperationInfo in scaland. Reference WI-288 (delivered: item 3, typeExprToRef arrow/tuple). Rust is ground truth. Acceptance: sbt test green; new LoaderTest cases asserting OperationInfo fact shape (incl. type_params) and let_expr.type_name / apply.type_args round-trip; parity with rustland load_operation on a small fixture."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-288", "WI-674"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
